{"format":1,"seq":56,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm tracing a bug where the model returns function_call items with raw source in the arguments even though the tool expects grammar-based input, and considering whether the recovery/display logic in display-input.ts—including the validation coercion that pulled in the pi-ai peer dependency—can be simplified while still showing users the coerced options Pi will actually execute.\n\nI'm wondering whether displayInputResolved could be avoided entirely by having the resolver just substitute recovered source into args directly, letting displayArguments handle the rest—eliminating the cache and prepareDisplayInput. But then I notice the partial-streaming test expects showing both the label and raw source line while a call is still streaming, which seems like new behavior beyond the original fix rather than existing logic, so this might be scope creep I need to flag.\n\nFor a minimal fix, I'm leaning toward just substituting recovered code into args when missing inside renderCall/renderResult, letting existing displayArguments logic apply options as normal, which is a small change. That would let me drop display-input.ts and displayInputResolved, but I need to check whether raw-call-recovery's type-only import from pi-ai is safe given it's not a direct dependency—maybe I can source the type from pi-coding-agent's ExtensionAPI message event instead.\n\nThe context handler that repairs old persisted history matters too: sessions recorded before this fix may contain broken function calls with empty arguments that would serialize incorrectly on replay and break the next request, so keeping that repair hook seems worthwhile, and I could unify it with the message_end hook to share the same recovery logic.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_018bxRBH4dgjjj1dBChiGtg2","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Check pi-ai usage in src, package deps, and Pi interactive row arg updates\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`grep -rn \"pi-ai\" src test/support --include=*.ts | grep -v raw- | head; echo ---; node -e 'const p=require(\"./package.json\");console.log(JSON.stringify({d:p.dependencies,dd:p.devDependencies,pd:p.peerDependencies}))'; echo ---; f=$(grep -rln \"updateArgs\" node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist --include=*.js | grep -v bundle | head -5); echo \"$f\"; for x in $f; do grep -n \"updateArgs\\\\|setArgsComplete\\\\|markExecutionStarted\" $x | head -20; done`);\n  return r.stdout + r.stderr;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1893,"cacheRead":37810,"cacheWrite":16982,"totalTokens":56687,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1543},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1795130886092,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_2ugtveijwtjrvvj6bq5h5gjlk2fyfqb7ss7kz2ae5rrctsl3urmq","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":21166,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":29,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":28}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":28,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant":29,"tools":[30],"pending":[]},"on":[30],"policy":"allSettled"},"startedAt":1795130886063}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":30,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.tool","version":3,"input":{"kind":"model","assistant":29,"callId":"toolu_bdrk_018bxRBH4dgjjj1dBChiGtg2"},"owner":28,"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"pending","checkpoint":{"phase":"call"}}}},{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"base","value":{"run":{"taskId":28,"inputs":[8],"turns":5,"first":7},"tools":[{"callId":"toolu_bdrk_018bxRBH4dgjjj1dBChiGtg